import sys
p=sys.argv[1]+"/README.md";s=open(p).read()
a="**Pack consolidation (`consolidate`, 2026-11-14).**"
assert s.count(a)==1
n='''**Pack gate (2026-11-14).** Full repacks by git clients on workers (a GUI opened on a worker, `git gc`) sent 4 GB packs to every machine and to the store and coincided with watchdog kills. The rule now lives in the replica boundary (`FleetIgnoreV1.local`, set by `guarded` from `🔁️replica/🧷️packgate`): a file of `.git/objects/pack` is shared only when the fleet register already holds its `.pack` or the consolidator authorised its stem (`.git/semio-packs.json`, written by `consolidate` before it places a pack; the very first machine seeds its packs while the fleet holds none); `multi-pack-index`, unknown names and everything below `.git/objects/info` (pack list, commit graphs) never leave a machine. A delete under `.git/objects` is published only for stems the consolidator authorised to retire; any other delete (a client `repack -ad` removing the fleet's packs, `prune-packed` removing loose objects) is not published and the heal brings the file back. Applying a deletion never removes `.git/refs`, `.git/refs/heads`, `.git/refs/tags`, `.git/objects`, `.git/objects/pack` or `.git/objects/info` (a `git gc` that packs the refs empties them and git then does not recognise the repository). Every 60 s (`rescueMilliseconds`) the daemon examines the complete packs this machine holds and the fleet does not: each object that no fleet pack holds and no loose file exists for is written as a loose object (the replica publishes it like any file), then the local pack is deleted (`rescueLocalPacksV1`); dead fragments older than an hour go too. The consolidator writes `<stem>.keep` (`semio-consolidated`) next to its pack, so `git repack -a -d` and `git gc` on any machine leave the fleet's pack alone. Tests (`🔁️replica/🧪️tests/🧷️packgate.ts`, real git, two daemons): `git repack -a -d` and `git gc --aggressive --prune=now` on a worker publish no event under `.git/objects/pack` or `.git/objects/info`, publish no pack delete, a commit made before the repack still reaches the server (through the rescue), both repositories pass `git fsck --full` and only the fleet's pack remains; the consolidator's pack arrives with its keep marker and a worker `repack -a -d` leaves it.

'''
s=s.replace(a,n+a)
open(p,"w").write(s)
